WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:05.610
In this section, we'll be adding code to our Blueprint actor within the Blueprint's

2
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.730
Event Graph.

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.250
The Event Graph executes commands at runtime during gameplay.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.410
So back on our project, I have the BP Sequence Trigger Box example open, and I'm under

5
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.859
the Event Graph tab.

6
00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.980
So the first thing we need to do is ensure that the BP Bot, which is our main

7
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.980
character, is the only actor that can trigger the sequence.

8
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.859
We'll do this by adding a Cast To node after the actor Begin Overlap.

9
00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:38.700
So to do that, I'm going to drag off of the Event Actor Begin Overlap, and just start

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.700
typing Cast To BP Bot.

11
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.189
There we have our Cast To BP Bot.

12
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:50.189
Next we're going to drag off this other actor and select the object.

13
00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.770
Compile and Save.

14
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.719
We should be good to go.

15
00:00:54.719 --> 00:01:01.240
Now next, from the Cast To BP Bot, we'll need to add a Set Actor Enable Collision node and

16
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.240
set it to false.

17
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:10.989
So to do that, we can just drag off of this, and we'll do Set Actor Collision.

18
00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:15.060
So there's our Set Actor Enable Collision, drag off of this, and we'll see that our

19
00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.939
new Actor Enable Collision is set to false.

20
00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:20.109
This is what we want.

21
00:01:20.109 --> 00:01:24.989
This will ensure that the BP Bot actor won't retrigger the event again once it's been

22
00:01:24.989 --> 00:01:25.989
activated.

23
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:32.510
A quick note here is as you're dragging off, if you don't see the Set Actor, you can

24
00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:37.709
uncheck Context Sensitive to see all of the nodes that are available.

25
00:01:37.709 --> 00:01:42.189
Context Sensitive is just a nice way of the engine filtering out results that typically

26
00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:46.230
work with this actor, but sometimes it gets it right, sometimes it doesn't.

27
00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.120
Go ahead and hit Compile.

28
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.079
Now the next thing we're going to do is create a new Level Sequence Actor object

29
00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.159
reference variable called Main Sequence.

30
00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:00.959
So underneath the variables, let's click our plus, a new variable, and let's just

31
00:02:00.959 --> 00:02:06.480
call this Main Sequence.

32
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.199
Now in my case, you can see that it did select it, but if your shows as, say, for

33
00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:15.159
example, a Boolean, all we need to do is just go up to Variable Type in the Details

34
00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:23.240
panel, select the dropdown, and then search for Level Sequence Actor, and you see

35
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.819
we have Level Sequence Actor, and we're going to select Object Reference.

36
00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:32.620
And the next thing we'll do in our Details panel is ensure that our blueprint is

37
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.259
instanced editable.

38
00:02:34.259 --> 00:02:38.300
So what this means is this variable that we've created will be exposed on our

39
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.699
blueprint when it's added to the level, meaning that we can change whatever this

40
00:02:42.699 --> 00:02:44.819
is referencing per instance.

41
00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:48.289
Let's go ahead and hit Compile.

42
00:02:48.289 --> 00:02:53.349
And now what we're going to do is after our Set Actor Enable Collision, we are going

43
00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:58.189
to create a new variable called, I'm sorry, not new variable, we're going to create

44
00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:00.990
a new node called Play.

45
00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:09.300
So if I do Play, uncheck Context Sensitive, and what I'm going to do is Play Sequence.

46
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.460
And what we're looking for is the Play, not Play Sequence, but Play.

47
00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.020
And it should say Target is Movie Scene Sequence Player.

48
00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.419
There we go.

49
00:03:20.419 --> 00:03:25.300
And then I'm going to drag my Main Sequence off onto our Target, and you'll see that

50
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.569
it automatically creates our translator here.

51
00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:34.330
So it's going to take our Main Sequence variable and plug it into the target of our

52
00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.330
Play.

53
00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.330
Perfect.

54
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.319
Let's go ahead and hit Compile.

55
00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:43.479
And then the last thing that we need to do is create a Boolean variable called IsPlaying.

56
00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:47.039
Now this variable is going to be used to check that the sequence is playing.

57
00:03:47.039 --> 00:03:52.719
And we'll also be able to use this logic to pause gameplay or trigger other events

58
00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:53.719
or logic.

59
00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:55.560
Let's go back down to our variables.

60
00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.560
Click our Plus.

61
00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.259
I'm going to call this IsPlaying.

62
00:04:01.259 --> 00:04:05.219
And we're going to change our Level Sequence Actor to a Boolean.

63
00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:06.219
There we go.

64
00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:09.000
We'll hit Compile and Save.

65
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.740
Now that our IsPlaying Boolean variable is created, we're going to drag and drop this

66
00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.620
into the Event Graph.

67
00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.339
And we're going to do the SetIsPlaying.

68
00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:22.699
We'll go ahead and drag off of our Play, connect it, and then we're going to check

69
00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:24.620
this that it is playing.

70
00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.879
We're going to hit Compile and Save.

71
00:04:28.879 --> 00:04:32.040
Now in the next section, we'll focus on pausing the actual sequence.
